Found under k21. lib/Dist/Zilla/Plugin/Author/GETTY/Binary.pm runs binary_pp_args as open "-|", "sh", "-c", $pp_args (~line 139) and verify/smoke as system("sh", "-c", "$cmd \"\$@\"", "sh", $out) (~line 155). On MSWin32 Perl joins the list into one CreateProcess command line and wraps an argument in " only when it has whitespace and no " - an embedded " is never escaped (win32/win32.c create_command_line, 5.40.1). The MSYS2 sh then re-parses that line with rules of its own (git-for-windows msys2-runtime dcrt0.cc build_argv/quoted/globify: single quotes quote too, \\ becomes \, words with ?*[\"(){} are globbed). verify/smoke always carry a " in the script, so a local "dzil build" with binary keys on native Windows perl mangles them; pp_args only when the command holds a ". The CI legs are not affected (k21 fixed pp-args.pl; build-leg.sh hook() is MSYS-to-MSYS). Fix shape as in pp-args.pl run_in_win32: hand the command over through the environment and run a fixed script without " or \.

